@startuml
title Login - POST /api/auth/login
hide footbox
actor Client
participant AuthController
participant AuthService
participant AppUserRepository
participant PasswordEncoder
participant JwtUtil
participant GlobalExceptionHandler as GEH

Client -> AuthController: POST /api/auth/login {username, password}
note right of Client: /api/auth/** is permitAll (no token required)

alt Request body fails @Valid (blank username or password)
    AuthController --> GEH: MethodArgumentNotValidException
    GEH --> Client: 400 Bad Request (field errors)
else Request body is valid
    AuthController -> AuthService: login(request)
    AuthService -> AppUserRepository: findByUsername(username)
    AppUserRepository --> AuthService: Optional<AppUser>

    alt Optional is empty (user not found)
        AuthService --> AuthController: throw BadCredentialsException
        AuthController --> GEH: BadCredentialsException
        GEH --> Client: 401 Unauthorized ("Invalid username or password")
    else User found
        AuthService -> PasswordEncoder: matches(request.getPassword(), user.getPassword())
        PasswordEncoder --> AuthService: boolean

        alt matches == false
            AuthService --> AuthController: throw BadCredentialsException
            AuthController --> GEH: BadCredentialsException
            GEH --> Client: 401 Unauthorized ("Invalid username or password")
        else matches == true
            alt user.getStatus() != ACTIVE
                AuthService --> AuthController: throw BadCredentialsException (account is inactive)
                AuthController --> GEH: BadCredentialsException
                GEH --> Client: 401 Unauthorized ("Invalid username or password")
                note right of GEH: The handler always returns the generic message,\nso the "inactive" message is never exposed
            else user.getStatus() == ACTIVE
                AuthService -> JwtUtil: generateToken(userId, username, role.name())
                JwtUtil --> AuthService: token
                AuthService --> AuthController: LoginResponse(token, "Bearer", userId, username, role)
                AuthController --> Client: 200 OK (LoginResponse)
            end
        end
    end
end
@enduml